From: G965N port maintainers
Subject: Preserve the keysym of GNOME on-screen keys without a hardware keycode

GNOME 46 InputMethod.handleVirtualKey passes keycode zero. Mapping that code
through the US hardware keymap discards the supplied letter, so the engine
rejects the event and GNOME falls back to Latin input. Keep hardware layout
normalization for nonzero codes and honor the supplied virtual keysym.
Based on Ubuntu ibus-hangul 1.5.5-2build2, upstream libhangul/ibus-hangul.
Original source notices and debian/copyright must be retained.

--- a/src/engine.c
+++ b/src/engine.c
@@ -1508 +1508 @@
-	    if (keymap != NULL)
+	    if (keymap != NULL && keycode != 0)
